From: u1eafd5d24fb29c12 at groups.google.com (David Champagne)
Date: Wed, 14 May 2014 19:43:27 +0000
Subject: Re: hdfs.read() of rhdfs-1.0.8 cannot load all data from huge csv file on hdfs?
Message-ID: <GmPuA9SM-04.UgUFGJCcMuwJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <GmPuA9SM-04.lAeJwY8YmyAJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
References: <GmPuA9SM-04.lAeJwY8YmyAJ@rhadoop.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rhadoop/c/GmPuA9SM-04/m/UgUFGJCcMuwJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rhdfs uses the java api for reading files stored in hdfs.  That api will not necessarily read the entire file in one shot.  It will return some number  of bytes for each read.  When it reaches the end of the file it returns -1.  In the case of rhdfs, and end of the file will return NULL.  So, you need to loop on the hdfs.read call until NULL is returned

